---
title: "Support"
description: "Get help with connections, transfers and your workspace."
---

## Contact the Serlink team

Use the form below for product help, problem reports, suggestions or privacy requests. A Serlink account is not required. Keep the reference shown after sending.

<SupportForm locale="en" />

For a reproducible public bug or feature request, use [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/backrunner/Serlink/issues). Issues are public; use the support form for private reports.

## Include the useful details

- Serlink version and operating system version.
- The action that failed and the approximate time.
- Whether this is an App Store or direct build.
- Relevant redacted diagnostic text, if it helps. This form has no file upload.

Diagnostic exports are available in **Settings → Diagnostic logs**. Review them before sending. Do not include passwords, private keys, recovery keys, MCP tokens or private terminal output.

## Try a guide first

[Connection troubleshooting](/docs/troubleshooting), [vault recovery](/docs/vault) and [sync guidance](/docs/sync) cover common issues. Check [release availability](/download) if you cannot find an installer.

The form sends only the information you enter. It does not automatically upload diagnostics, terminal output or vault data. See [privacy](/privacy) for support data handling.

## iPhone and iPad transfers

Use the document picker to upload and the share sheet to open or save downloaded files. External edits do not automatically upload. Keep Serlink open during transfers; background completion is not guaranteed. Local shells, OS SSH-agent authentication and desktop split panes are not iOS features.
